affiliation={Key Laboratory of Electronics and Information Technology for Space Systems, Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, 100190, China; Tianjin Key Laboratory of Wireless Mobile Communications and Power Transmission, Tianjin Normal University, Tianjin, 300387, China; Department of Electronic and Information Engineering, North China University of Technology, Beijing, 100144, China},
abstract={Visual simultaneous localization and mapping (V-SLAM) technique plays a key role in perception of autonomous mobile robots, augmented/mixed/virtual reality, as well as spatial AI applications. This paper gives a very concise survey about the front-end module of a V-SLAM system, which is charge of feature extraction, short/long-term data association with outlier rejection, as well as variable initialization. Visual features are mainly salient and repeatable points, called keypoints, their traditional extractors and matchers are hand-engineered and not robust to viewpoint/illumination/seasonal change, which is crucial for long-term autonomy of mobile robots. Therefore, new trend about deep-learning-based keypoint extractors and matchers are introduced to enhance the robustness of V-SLAM systems even under challenging conditions. © 2022, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd.},
